{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Anomaly Detection Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code in `code/anomaly_detection.py` implements Z-score, IQR, and Isolation Forest from scratch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Z-Score Detector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def zscore_detect(X, threshold=3.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mean = X.mean(axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    std = X.std(axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    std[std == 0] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    z = np.abs((X - mean) / std)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return z.max(axis=1) > threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simple and vectorized. Flags a point if any feature exceeds the threshold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### IQR Detector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def iqr_detect(X, factor=1.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    q1 = np.percentile(X, 25, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    q3 = np.percentile(X, 75, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    iqr = q3 - q1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    iqr[iqr == 0] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lower = q1 - factor * iqr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    upper = q3 + factor * iqr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outside = (X < lower) | (X > upper)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return outside.any(axis=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Isolation Forest from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The from-scratch implementation builds isolation trees that randomly partition the feature space:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class IsolationTree:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, max_depth):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_depth = max_depth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, depth=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n, p = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if depth >= self.max_depth or n <= 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.is_leaf = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.size = n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.is_leaf = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.feature = np.random.randint(p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_min = X[:, self.feature].min()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_max = X[:, self.feature].max()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if x_min == x_max:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.is_leaf = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.size = n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.threshold = np.random.uniform(x_min, x_max)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        left_mask = X[:, self.feature] < self.threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.left = IsolationTree(self.max_depth).fit(X[left_mask], depth + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.right = IsolationTree(self.max_depth).fit(X[~left_mask], depth + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The path length to isolate a point determines its anomaly score. Shorter paths mean more anomalous."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `IsolationForest` class wraps multiple trees:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class IsolationForest:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_estimators=100, max_samples=256, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_estimators = n_estimators"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_samples = max_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sample_size = min(self.max_samples, X.shape[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_depth = int(np.ceil(np.log2(sample_size)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(self.n_estimators):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            idx = rng.choice(X.shape[0], size=sample_size, replace=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree = IsolationTree(max_depth=max_depth)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree.fit(X[idx])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.trees.append(tree)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def anomaly_score(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_path = average path length across all trees"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores = 2.0 ** (-avg_path / c(max_samples))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The normalization factor `c(n)` is the expected path length of an unsuccessful search in a binary search tree with n elements. It equals `2 * H(n-1) - 2*(n-1)/n` where `H` is the harmonic number. This normalization ensures scores are comparable across datasets of different sizes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Demo Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code generates multiple test scenarios:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. **Single cluster with outliers.** A 2D Gaussian cluster with anomalies injected far from the center. All methods should work here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. **Multimodal data.** Three clusters of different sizes and densities. Points between clusters are anomalous. Z-score struggles because the per-feature ranges are wide."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. **High-dimensional data.** 50 features, but anomalies differ in only 5 of them. Tests whether methods can find anomalies in a subset of features."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each demo compares all methods using precision, recall, F1, and Precision@k."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Threshold tuning.** Run the Z-score detector with thresholds from 1.0 to 5.0 in steps of 0.5. Plot precision and recall at each threshold. Where is the sweet spot for your data?\n\n2. **Multivariate anomalies.** Create 2D data where each feature individually looks normal, but the combination is anomalous (e.g., points far from the main cluster diagonal). Show that Z-score per feature misses these but Isolation Forest catches them.\n\n3. **LOF from scratch.** Implement Local Outlier Factor using k-nearest neighbors. Compare against sklearn's LocalOutlierFactor on the same data. Use k=10 and k=50 -- how does the choice of k affect results?\n\n4. **Streaming anomaly detection.** Modify the Z-score detector to work in a streaming setting: update the running mean and variance as new points arrive (Welford's online algorithm). Compare to batch Z-score on the same data.\n\n5. **Real-world evaluation.** Take a dataset with known anomalies (credit card fraud from Kaggle, for example). Evaluate all four methods using precision@100, precision@500, and AUPRC. Which method works best? Why?"
      ]
    }
